"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkgodot_iap_docs=globalThis.webpackChunkgodot_iap_docs||[]).push([[6471],{5798(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"1.2.4","metadata":{"permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.2.4","editUrl":"https://github.com/hyochan/godot-iap/tree/main/docs/blog/2026-02-11-1.2.4.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-02-11-1.2.4.md","title":"1.2.4 - OpenIAP 1.3.17 Sync","description":"This release syncs with OpenIAP v1.3.17, adding new types for Google Play Billing Library 5.0+ and 7.0+ features.","date":"2026-02-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/release","description":"New version releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"OpenIAP","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/openiap","description":"OpenIAP integration updates"},{"inline":false,"label":"Android","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/android","description":"Android-specific updates"},{"inline":true,"label":"billing-library","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/billing-library"}],"readingTime":0.9,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Hyo","title":"Godot IAP Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/hyochan","page":{"permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/authors/hyochan"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/hyochan","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/hyochanjang/","x":"https://x.com/hyodotdev"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/hyochan.png","key":"hyochan"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"1.2.4","title":"1.2.4 - OpenIAP 1.3.17 Sync","authors":["hyochan"],"tags":["release","openiap","android","billing-library"],"date":"2026-02-11T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"1.2.3 - ExternalPurchaseCustomLink Types (iOS 18.1+)","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.2.3-external-purchase-custom-link"}},"content":"This release syncs with [OpenIAP v1.3.17](https://www.openiap.dev/docs/updates/notes#gql-1317), adding new types for Google Play Billing Library 5.0+ and 7.0+ features.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## New Types\\n\\n### InstallmentPlanDetailsAndroid (Billing Library 7.0+)\\n\\nSubscription installment plan details for plans that allow users to pay in installments.\\n\\n```gdscript\\nclass InstallmentPlanDetailsAndroid:\\n    ## Committed payments count after signup (e.g., 12 monthly payments)\\n    var commitment_payments_count: int\\n    ## Subsequent commitment payments when plan renews (0 if reverts to normal)\\n    var subsequent_commitment_payments_count: int\\n```\\n\\nThis is available on `ProductSubscriptionAndroidOfferDetails.installment_plan_details`.\\n\\n### PendingPurchaseUpdateAndroid (Billing Library 5.0+)\\n\\nDetails about pending subscription upgrades/downgrades.\\n\\n```gdscript\\nclass PendingPurchaseUpdateAndroid:\\n    ## Product IDs for the pending purchase update\\n    var products: Array[String]\\n    ## Purchase token for the pending transaction\\n    var purchase_token: String\\n```\\n\\nThis is available on `PurchaseAndroid.pending_purchase_update_android`.\\n\\n### purchase_option_id_android (Billing Library 7.0+)\\n\\nNew field on `DiscountOffer` and `ProductAndroidOneTimePurchaseOfferDetail` to identify which purchase option the user selected.\\n\\n```gdscript\\n# Available on DiscountOffer\\ndiscount_offer.purchase_option_id_android # String or null\\n```\\n\\n## OpenIAP Versions\\n\\n| Package | Version |\\n|---------|---------|\\n| openiap-gql | 1.3.17 |\\n| openiap-google | 1.3.28 |\\n| openiap-apple | 1.3.14 |\\n\\n## Installation\\n\\nDownload from [Asset Library](https://godotengine.org/asset-library/) or clone from GitHub.\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- [OpenIAP Release Notes](https://www.openiap.dev/docs/updates/notes#gql-1317)"},{"id":"1.2.3-external-purchase-custom-link","metadata":{"permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.2.3-external-purchase-custom-link","editUrl":"https://github.com/hyochan/godot-iap/tree/main/docs/blog/2026-01-26-1.2.3.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-01-26-1.2.3.md","title":"1.2.3 - ExternalPurchaseCustomLink Types (iOS 18.1+)","description":"This release syncs with OpenIAP v1.3.16 and adds type support for the new ExternalPurchaseCustomLink API introduced in iOS 18.1.","date":"2026-01-26T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/release","description":"New version releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"OpenIAP","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/openiap","description":"OpenIAP integration updates"},{"inline":false,"label":"iOS","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/ios","description":"iOS-specific updates"},{"inline":true,"label":"storekit","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/storekit"}],"readingTime":1.14,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Hyo","title":"Godot IAP Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/hyochan","page":{"permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/authors/hyochan"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/hyochan","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/hyochanjang/","x":"https://x.com/hyodotdev"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/hyochan.png","key":"hyochan"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"1.2.3-external-purchase-custom-link","title":"1.2.3 - ExternalPurchaseCustomLink Types (iOS 18.1+)","authors":["hyochan"],"tags":["release","openiap","ios","storekit"],"date":"2026-01-26T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"1.2.4 - OpenIAP 1.3.17 Sync","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.2.4"},"nextItem":{"title":"1.2.0 - Android Input Type Field Naming Simplification","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.2.0-offertoken-naming"}},"content":"This release syncs with [OpenIAP v1.3.16](https://www.openiap.dev/docs/updates/notes#1316) and adds type support for the new ExternalPurchaseCustomLink API introduced in iOS 18.1.\\n\\n## New Types\\n\\n### ExternalPurchaseCustomLink API Types (iOS 18.1+)\\n\\nThis release adds GDScript type definitions for Apple\'s new ExternalPurchaseCustomLink API, which allows developers to direct users to external purchase links with proper tracking.\\n\\n**New Enums:**\\n\\n```gdscript\\n# Notice type for showing external purchase disclosure\\nenum ExternalPurchaseCustomLinkNoticeTypeIOS {\\n    BROWSER = 0,  # Display notice for browser-based purchases\\n}\\n\\n# Token type for tracking external purchases\\nenum ExternalPurchaseCustomLinkTokenTypeIOS {\\n    ACQUISITION = 0,  # For new customer acquisition tracking\\n    SERVICES = 1,     # For existing customer services tracking\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**New Result Types:**\\n\\n```gdscript\\n# Result from showing the notice sheet\\nclass ExternalPurchaseCustomLinkNoticeResultIOS:\\n    var continued: bool  # True if user chose to continue\\n    var error: String    # Error message if presentation failed\\n\\n# Result from requesting a token\\nclass ExternalPurchaseCustomLinkTokenResultIOS:\\n    var token: String    # The external purchase token\\n    var error: String    # Error message if retrieval failed\\n```\\n\\n### iOS Version Corrections\\n\\n- ExternalPurchase API availability corrected to iOS 17.4+ (was incorrectly marked as 18.2+ in some cases)\\n\\n## Note\\n\\nThis is a **type-only release**. The native wrapper functions for ExternalPurchaseCustomLink API are not yet exposed in godot-iap. The types are available for future integration or manual native bridge calls.\\n\\n## OpenIAP Versions\\n\\n| Package | Version |\\n|---------|---------|\\n| openiap-gql | 1.3.16 |\\n| openiap-google | 1.3.27 |\\n| openiap-apple | 1.3.14 |\\n\\nFor detailed changes, see the [OpenIAP Release Notes](https://www.openiap.dev/docs/updates/notes#1316)."},{"id":"1.2.0-offertoken-naming","metadata":{"permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.2.0-offertoken-naming","editUrl":"https://github.com/hyochan/godot-iap/tree/main/docs/blog/2026-01-20-1.2.0.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-01-20-1.2.0.md","title":"1.2.0 - Android Input Type Field Naming Simplification","description":"This release syncs with OpenIAP v1.3.15 and simplifies field naming in Android input types.","date":"2026-01-20T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/release","description":"New version releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"OpenIAP","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/openiap","description":"OpenIAP integration updates"},{"inline":false,"label":"Android","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/android","description":"Android-specific updates"},{"inline":true,"label":"billing","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/billing"},{"inline":false,"label":"Breaking Change","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/breaking-change","description":"Breaking changes that require migration"}],"readingTime":1.36,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Hyo","title":"Godot IAP Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/hyochan","page":{"permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/authors/hyochan"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/hyochan","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/hyochanjang/","x":"https://x.com/hyodotdev"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/hyochan.png","key":"hyochan"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"1.2.0-offertoken-naming","title":"1.2.0 - Android Input Type Field Naming Simplification","authors":["hyochan"],"tags":["release","openiap","android","billing","breaking-change"],"date":"2026-01-20T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"1.2.3 - ExternalPurchaseCustomLink Types (iOS 18.1+)","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.2.3-external-purchase-custom-link"},"nextItem":{"title":"1.1.1 \u2014 OpenIAP 1.3.14 & New Android/iOS Types","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.1.1"}},"content":"This release syncs with [OpenIAP v1.3.15](https://www.openiap.dev/docs/updates/notes#1315) and simplifies field naming in Android input types.\\n\\n## New Features\\n\\n### One-Time Purchase Discount Offers (Android 7.0+)\\n\\nYou can now apply discount offers to one-time (in-app) purchases using `offer_token`:\\n\\n```gdscript\\n# Get product with discount offers\\nvar products = await iap.get_products([\\"premium_upgrade\\"], \\"inapp\\")\\nvar product = products[0]\\n\\n# Check for discount offers\\nif product.discount_offers.size() > 0:\\n    var offer = product.discount_offers[0]\\n\\n    # Purchase with discount\\n    var request = RequestPurchaseAndroidProps.new()\\n    request.skus = [\\"premium_upgrade\\"]\\n    request.offer_token = offer.offer_token_android\\n\\n    var result = await iap.request_purchase_android(request)\\n```\\n\\n## Breaking Changes\\n\\n### Simplified Field Names in Android Input Types\\n\\nFields inside platform-specific input types no longer require the `_android` suffix. The parent type name already indicates the platform context.\\n\\n**Why this change?**\\n\\nWhen you use `RequestPurchaseAndroidProps`, the type name already tells you this is Android-specific. Adding `_android` suffix to fields inside is redundant.\\n\\n### Migration Guide\\n\\n| Old Name | New Name |\\n|----------|----------|\\n| `obfuscated_account_id_android` | `obfuscated_account_id` |\\n| `obfuscated_profile_id_android` | `obfuscated_profile_id` |\\n| `purchase_token_android` | `purchase_token` |\\n| `replacement_mode_android` | `replacement_mode` |\\n\\n**Before:**\\n\\n```gdscript\\nvar request = RequestSubscriptionAndroidProps.new()\\nrequest.skus = [\\"premium_monthly\\"]\\nrequest.obfuscated_account_id_android = \\"user_123\\"\\nrequest.purchase_token_android = old_token\\nrequest.replacement_mode_android = 2\\n```\\n\\n**After:**\\n\\n```gdscript\\nvar request = RequestSubscriptionAndroidProps.new()\\nrequest.skus = [\\"premium_monthly\\"]\\nrequest.obfuscated_account_id = \\"user_123\\"\\nrequest.purchase_token = old_token\\nrequest.replacement_mode = 2\\n```\\n\\n### Important: Response Types Keep Suffixes\\n\\nThe suffix removal only applies to **input types** (request parameters). Response types still use suffixes because they\'re cross-platform:\\n\\n```gdscript\\n# Response fields KEEP the _android suffix\\nvar offer = product.discount_offers[0]\\nvar token = offer.offer_token_android  # Response field - keeps suffix\\n\\n# Input fields DON\'T have suffix\\nvar request = RequestPurchaseAndroidProps.new()\\nrequest.offer_token = token  # Input field - no suffix\\n```\\n\\n## Bug Fixes\\n\\n- Fix GDScript enum reverse lookup for deserialization\\n\\n## OpenIAP Versions\\n\\n| Package | Version |\\n|---------|---------|\\n| openiap-gql | 1.3.15 |\\n| openiap-google | 1.3.26 |\\n| openiap-apple | 1.3.13 |\\n\\nFor detailed changes, see the [OpenIAP Release Notes](https://www.openiap.dev/docs/updates/notes#1315)."},{"id":"1.1.1","metadata":{"permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.1.1","editUrl":"https://github.com/hyochan/godot-iap/tree/main/docs/blog/2026-01-18-1.1.1.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-01-18-1.1.1.md","title":"1.1.1 \u2014 OpenIAP 1.3.14 & New Android/iOS Types","description":"Godot IAP 1.1.1 syncs with OpenIAP v1.3.14, bringing new enums, types, and subscription features for both Android and iOS platforms.","date":"2026-01-18T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/release","description":"New version releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Android","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/android","description":"Android-specific updates"},{"inline":false,"label":"iOS","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/ios","description":"iOS-specific updates"},{"inline":false,"label":"OpenIAP","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/openiap","description":"OpenIAP integration updates"}],"readingTime":1.75,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Hyo","title":"Godot IAP Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/hyochan","page":{"permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/authors/hyochan"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/hyochan","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/hyochanjang/","x":"https://x.com/hyodotdev"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/hyochan.png","key":"hyochan"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"1.1.1","title":"1.1.1 \u2014 OpenIAP 1.3.14 & New Android/iOS Types","tags":["release","android","ios","openiap"],"authors":["hyochan"],"date":"2026-01-18T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"1.2.0 - Android Input Type Field Naming Simplification","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.2.0-offertoken-naming"},"nextItem":{"title":"1.1.0 \u2014 macOS Support & OpenIAP 1.3.12","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.1.0"}},"content":"Godot IAP 1.1.1 syncs with OpenIAP v1.3.14, bringing new enums, types, and subscription features for both Android and iOS platforms.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nimport IapKitBanner from \\"@site/src/uis/IapKitBanner\\";\\n\\n<IapKitBanner />\\n\\n## Highlights\\n\\n- **New Android Enums**: ProductStatusAndroid and SubResponseCodeAndroid for granular error handling\\n- **iOS Win-Back Offers**: Type support for iOS 18+ win-back offers\\n- **JWS Promotional Offers**: New iOS promotional offer format\\n- **Kotlin Warning Fixes**: Resolved type inference warnings for nullable strings\\n\\n## New Android Features (Billing Library 8.0+)\\n\\n### ProductStatusAndroid Enum\\n\\nIndividual product fetch status codes:\\n\\n```gdscript\\nenum ProductStatusAndroid {\\n    OK,                    # Product was successfully fetched\\n    NOT_FOUND,             # Product SKU doesn\'t exist in Play Console\\n    NO_OFFERS_AVAILABLE,   # Product exists but user is not eligible\\n    UNKNOWN                # Unknown error occurred\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### SubResponseCodeAndroid Enum\\n\\nGranular purchase error information:\\n\\n```gdscript\\nenum SubResponseCodeAndroid {\\n    NO_APPLICABLE_SUB_RESPONSE_CODE,              # No specific sub-response code\\n    PAYMENT_DECLINED_DUE_TO_INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS,   # Insufficient funds\\n    USER_INELIGIBLE                               # User doesn\'t meet eligibility\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### BillingResultAndroid Class\\n\\nExtended billing result with sub-response code for detailed error handling.\\n\\n## New iOS Features\\n\\n### Win-Back Offers (iOS 18+)\\n\\nNew `SubscriptionOfferTypeIOS.WIN_BACK` offer type for re-engaging churned subscribers:\\n\\n```gdscript\\n# Type support for win-back offers\\nvar props = Types.RequestSubscriptionIosProps.new()\\nprops.win_back_offer = win_back_offer_input\\n```\\n\\n### JWS Promotional Offers (iOS 15+)\\n\\nNew `PromotionalOfferJWSInputIOS` class for JWS format promotional offers.\\n\\n### RequestSubscriptionIosProps New Fields\\n\\n- `win_back_offer`: Win-back offer to apply (iOS 18+)\\n- `promotional_offer_jws`: JWS promotional offer (iOS 15+)\\n- `introductory_offer_eligibility`: Override introductory offer eligibility\\n\\n## Android Improvements\\n\\n### RequestActiveSubscriptionsAndroidProps\\n\\nNew field `include_suspended_android` to include suspended subscriptions in results (Android 8.1+).\\n\\n### ProductAndroid\\n\\nNew field `product_status_android` for product-level status code indicating fetch result.\\n\\n## Bug Fixes\\n\\n- Resolved Kotlin type inference warnings for nullable strings in Android plugin\\n\\n## Version Updates\\n\\n| Package | Version |\\n|---------|---------|\\n| openiap-gql | 1.3.14 |\\n| openiap-apple | 1.3.12 |\\n| openiap-google | 1.3.25 |\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- iOS subscription features (win-back offers, JWS promotional offers) are **type-only updates**. Using them requires native GDExtension updates which will be added in a future release.\\n- Android enums (`ProductStatusAndroid`, `SubResponseCodeAndroid`) are returned automatically by OpenIAP when available.\\n\\n## Upgrade Guide\\n\\nNo breaking changes from 1.1.0:\\n\\n1. Download the latest release\\n2. Replace your `addons/godot-iap` folder\\n3. Rebuild your project\\n\\nFor detailed changes, see the [OpenIAP Release Notes](https://openiap.dev/docs/updates/notes#1314---standardized-offer-types).\\n\\nFollow for updates: [@hyodotdev](https://x.com/hyodotdev)"},{"id":"1.1.0","metadata":{"permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.1.0","editUrl":"https://github.com/hyochan/godot-iap/tree/main/docs/blog/2026-01-17-1.1.0.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-01-17-1.1.0.md","title":"1.1.0 \u2014 macOS Support & OpenIAP 1.3.12","description":"Godot IAP 1.1.0 adds macOS support and syncs with OpenIAP v1.3.12, bringing new features and improvements to both iOS and Android platforms.","date":"2026-01-17T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/release","description":"New version releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"macOS","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/macos","description":"macOS-specific updates"},{"inline":false,"label":"iOS","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/ios","description":"iOS-specific updates"},{"inline":false,"label":"Android","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/android","description":"Android-specific updates"},{"inline":false,"label":"OpenIAP","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/openiap","description":"OpenIAP integration updates"}],"readingTime":1.15,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Hyo","title":"Godot IAP Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/hyochan","page":{"permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/authors/hyochan"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/hyochan","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/hyochanjang/","x":"https://x.com/hyodotdev"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/hyochan.png","key":"hyochan"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"1.1.0","title":"1.1.0 \u2014 macOS Support & OpenIAP 1.3.12","tags":["release","macos","ios","android","openiap"],"authors":["hyochan"],"date":"2026-01-17T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"1.1.1 \u2014 OpenIAP 1.3.14 & New Android/iOS Types","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.1.1"},"nextItem":{"title":"1.0.0 \u2014 First Stable Release","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.0.0"}},"content":"Godot IAP 1.1.0 adds **macOS support** and syncs with OpenIAP v1.3.12, bringing new features and improvements to both iOS and Android platforms.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nimport IapKitBanner from \\"@site/src/uis/IapKitBanner\\";\\n\\n<IapKitBanner />\\n\\n## Highlights\\n\\n- **macOS Support**: GDExtension plugin now works on macOS\\n- **OpenIAP 1.3.12**: Updated native modules with latest features\\n- **Improved Documentation**: AI-friendly docs for LLM assistants\\n\\n## New: macOS Support\\n\\nThe GDExtension plugin now supports macOS alongside iOS. This enables:\\n\\n- Desktop game development with IAP\\n- Unified codebase for iOS and macOS\\n- Same StoreKit 2 API on both platforms\\n\\n### Platform Detection\\n\\n```gdscript\\nif OS.get_name() == \\"macOS\\":\\n    # macOS-specific handling\\n    pass\\nelif OS.get_name() == \\"iOS\\":\\n    # iOS-specific handling\\n    pass\\n```\\n\\n## OpenIAP Updates\\n\\nSynced with OpenIAP v1.3.12 which includes:\\n\\n### iOS Improvements (openiap-apple 1.3.12)\\n\\n- Enhanced transaction handling\\n- Improved error messages\\n- Better subscription status reporting\\n\\n### Android Improvements (openiap-google 1.3.22)\\n\\n- Updated to Google Play Billing Library 8.x improvements\\n- Better offer handling for subscriptions\\n- Improved purchase flow stability\\n\\n## Version Updates\\n\\n| Package | Version |\\n|---------|---------|\\n| openiap-apple | 1.3.12 |\\n| openiap-google | 1.3.22 |\\n\\n## Documentation Updates\\n\\n- Added AI-friendly documentation for LLM assistants (CLAUDE.md)\\n- Simplified README with documentation links\\n- Fixed Quick Start code examples\\n\\n## Upgrade Guide\\n\\nNo breaking changes from 1.0.0. Simply update the plugin:\\n\\n1. Download the latest release\\n2. Replace your `addons/godot-iap` folder\\n3. Rebuild your project\\n\\n## What\'s Next\\n\\n- Enhanced subscription management APIs\\n- Win-back offer support (iOS 18+)\\n- More platform-specific features\\n\\nFollow for updates: [@hyodotdev](https://x.com/hyodotdev)"},{"id":"1.0.0","metadata":{"permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.0.0","editUrl":"https://github.com/hyochan/godot-iap/tree/main/docs/blog/2026-01-01-1.0.0.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-01-01-1.0.0.md","title":"1.0.0 \u2014 First Stable Release","description":"We\'re excited to announce the first stable release of Godot IAP \u2014 a comprehensive in-app purchase plugin for Godot 4.x that conforms to the OpenIAP specification.","date":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/release","description":"New version releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Android","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/android","description":"Android-specific updates"},{"inline":false,"label":"iOS","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/ios","description":"iOS-specific updates"},{"inline":false,"label":"OpenIAP","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/tags/openiap","description":"OpenIAP integration updates"}],"readingTime":1.44,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Hyo","title":"Godot IAP Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/hyochan","page":{"permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/authors/hyochan"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/hyochan","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/hyochanjang/","x":"https://x.com/hyodotdev"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/hyochan.png","key":"hyochan"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"1.0.0","title":"1.0.0 \u2014 First Stable Release","tags":["release","android","ios","openiap"],"authors":["hyochan"],"date":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"1.1.0 \u2014 macOS Support & OpenIAP 1.3.12","permalink":"/godot-iap/blog/1.1.0"}},"content":"We\'re excited to announce the first stable release of **Godot IAP** \u2014 a comprehensive in-app purchase plugin for Godot 4.x that conforms to the [OpenIAP specification](https://openiap.dev).\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nimport IapKitBanner from \\"@site/src/uis/IapKitBanner\\";\\n\\n<IapKitBanner />\\n\\n## Highlights\\n\\nGodot IAP 1.0.0 brings production-ready IAP functionality to Godot games with:\\n\\n- **Type-safe GDScript API** with auto-generated types from OpenIAP GraphQL schema\\n- **StoreKit 2** for iOS with modern async/await patterns\\n- **Google Play Billing Library 8+** for Android\\n- **Unified interface** across both platforms\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n### Cross-Platform Support\\n\\n- iOS: StoreKit 2 with Transaction listeners\\n- Android: Google Play Billing Library 8.x\\n\\n### Type-Safe API\\n\\nAll API methods use typed parameters and return values:\\n\\n```gdscript\\nconst Types = preload(\\"res://addons/godot-iap/types.gd\\")\\n\\n# Fetch products with typed request\\nvar request = Types.ProductRequest.new()\\nrequest.skus = [\\"product_1\\", \\"product_2\\"]\\nvar products: Array = GodotIapPlugin.fetch_products(request)\\n\\n# Request purchase with typed props\\nvar props = Types.RequestPurchaseProps.new()\\nprops.sku = \\"product_1\\"\\nvar purchase = GodotIapPlugin.request_purchase(props)\\n```\\n\\n### Core Methods\\n\\n| Method | Description |\\n|--------|-------------|\\n| `init_connection()` | Initialize store connection |\\n| `end_connection()` | Close connection |\\n| `fetch_products(request)` | Get product information |\\n| `request_purchase(props)` | Start a purchase |\\n| `finish_transaction(purchase, is_consumable)` | Complete transaction |\\n| `restore_purchases()` | Restore previous purchases |\\n\\n### Signal-Based Events\\n\\n```gdscript\\nGodotIapPlugin.purchase_updated.connect(_on_purchase_updated)\\nGodotIapPlugin.purchase_error.connect(_on_purchase_error)\\n```\\n\\n## Getting Started\\n\\n1. Download from Godot Asset Library or GitHub releases\\n2. Copy `addons/godot-iap` to your project\\n3. Enable the plugin in Project Settings\\n4. Follow platform-specific setup guides\\n\\n## OpenIAP Integration\\n\\nGodot IAP is powered by [OpenIAP](https://openiap.dev) \u2014 a standardized IAP specification ensuring consistent behavior across platforms and SDKs.\\n\\n| Package | Version |\\n|---------|---------|\\n| openiap-apple | 1.3.6 |\\n| openiap-google | 1.3.17 |\\n\\n## Documentation\\n\\n- [Getting Started](/getting-started/installation)\\n- [API Reference](/api)\\n- [Examples](/examples/purchase-flow)\\n\\n## What\'s Next\\n\\nWe\'re working on additional features including:\\n\\n- macOS support\\n- More subscription management APIs\\n- Enhanced error handling\\n\\nFollow for updates: [@hyodotdev](https://x.com/hyodotdev)"}]}}')}}]);